"pending":[{"id":129,"army":"A6","prov":"RAE","destination":true,"turn":23}],"dispatches":[{"t":0,"loc":"DAL","text":"March, AD 68. Word comes from Gaul: Julius Vindex, governor of Lugdunensis, has risen against Nero."},{"t":0,"loc":"DAL","text":"XI Claudia takes your promises."},{"t":0,"loc":"LUG","text":"Julius Vindex, governor of Lugdunensis, raises the Gauls against Nero."},{"t":1,"loc":"DAL","text":"Dalmatia is yours."},{"t":1,"loc":"TAR","text":"At Hispania Tarraconensis, the old governor Servius Sulpicius Galba lets his men hail him: legate of the Senate and People, he says, not yet emperor."},{"t":1,"loc":"JUD","text":"Titus Arrius, legate of V Macedonica, claims the purple in Judaea."},{"t":2,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Gaius Julius Vindex and you."},{"t":2,"loc":"AFR","text":"In Africa, Clodius Macer, legate of III Augusta, holds back the grain ships and raises a legion of his own."},{"t":3,"loc":null,"text":"An alliance is agreed between Lucius Clodius Macer and you."},{"t":3,"loc":"ROM","text":"Nero is dead. Abandoned by the Praetorians, he took his own life outside Rome. The Senate rules, for now."},{"t":3,"loc":"EGY","text":"Quintus Numisius, legate of XXII Deiotariana, claims the purple in Aegyptus."},{"t":3,"loc":null,"text":"Titus Arrius has lost his last legion. His cause is finished."},{"t":5,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Gaius Julius Vindex and Lucius Clodius Macer."},{"t":6,"loc":"MCA","text":"The Mauretanian chiefs send 3000 men to Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":6,"loc":"MTI","text":"Lucius Clodius Macer buys New legion of Mauretania Caesariensis."},{"t":7,"loc":"GIN","text":"Sextus Arrius, legate of V Alaudae, claims the purple in Germania Inferior."},{"t":7,"loc":"SYR","text":"Antiochus IV of Commagene sends 4000 men to Quintus Numisius."},{"t":8,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Sextus Arrius and you."},{"t":9,"loc":null,"text":"Your legions hail you as imperator."},{"t":9,"loc":"MOE","text":"Publius Arrius, legate of III Gallica, claims the purple in Moesia."},{"t":9,"loc":"TAR","text":"Battle near Tarraco: Lucius Clodius Macer wins against Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":10,"loc":null,"text":"An alliance is agreed between Publius Arrius and you."},{"t":10,"loc":"GSU","text":"On the Rhine, the legions refuse their oath and hail Aulus Vitellius emperor."},{"t":10,"loc":"CMP","text":"Marcus Salvius Otho, once Nero's friend, buys the Praetorians and claims the throne."},{"t":11,"loc":"MOE","text":"The Roxolani cross the frozen Danube into Moesia."},{"t":11,"loc":"SYR","text":"Marcus Vipstanus, legate of XII Fulminata, claims the purple in Syria."},{"t":11,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Sextus Arrius and Aulus Vitellius."},{"t":11,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Aulus Vitellius and Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":11,"loc":"ROM","text":"On the eve of battle, V Macedonica goes over to Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":11,"loc":"ROM","text":"Battle near Roma: night falls with neither army broken. Quintus Numisius draws off."},{"t":12,"loc":"SYR","text":"Sohaemus of Emesa sends 3000 men to Quintus Numisius."},{"t":12,"loc":"NIT","text":"Aulus Vitellius buys I Italica."},{"t":13,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Marcus Vipstanus and Publius Arrius."},{"t":13,"loc":"TAR","text":"Servius Sulpicius Galba falls back from Hispania Tarraconensis rather than fight Lucius Clodius Macer."},{"t":14,"loc":"BRI","text":"In Britain, Venutius leads the Brigantes in revolt."},{"t":14,"loc":"BRI","text":"Gaius Tettius, legate of IX Hispana, claims the purple in Britannia."},{"t":14,"loc":"ACO","text":"The Alpine chiefs send 2000 men to Aulus Vitellius."},{"t":14,"loc":"ROM","text":"The Senate recognises Aulus Vitellius as emperor."},{"t":16,"loc":"CYP","text":"At Alexandria, the legions of the East hail Titus Flavius Vespasianus emperor. The last act begins."},{"t":16,"loc":"ASI","text":"Aulus Vitellius falls back from Asia rather than fight Titus Flavius Vespasianus."},{"t":17,"loc":"GIN","text":"On the Rhine, the Batavian prince Julius Civilis stirs his people."},{"t":17,"loc":"GIN","text":"The frontier breaks in Germania Inferior. Raiders burn the farms; no taxes will come from there for months."},{"t":17,"loc":"ROM","text":"On the eve of battle, V Macedonica goes over to Aulus Vitellius."},{"t":17,"loc":"ROM","text":"Battle near Roma: Servius Sulpicius Galba wins against Aulus Vitellius."},{"t":17,"loc":"ROM","text":"The Senate recognises Servius Sulpicius Galba as emperor."},{"t":19,"loc":"ROM","text":"On the eve of battle, V Macedonica goes over to Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":19,"loc":"ROM","text":"Battle near Roma: night falls with neither army broken. Aulus Vitellius draws off."},{"t":20,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Servius Sulpicius Galba and Titus Flavius Vespasianus."},{"t":20,"loc":null,"text":"An alliance is agreed between Marcus Salvius Otho and Titus Flavius Vespasianus."},{"t":21,"loc":null,"text":"A truce is agreed between Titus Flavius Vespasianus and you."},{"t":21,"loc":null,"text":"An alliance is agreed between Marcus Salvius Otho and Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":22,"loc":"AFR","text":"The Garamantes raid the coast of Africa."},{"t":22,"loc":"ROM","text":"On the eve of battle, V Macedonica goes over to Servius Sulpicius Galba."},{"t":22,"loc":"ROM","text":"Battle near Roma: night falls with neither army broken. Aulus Vitellius draws off."},{"t":22,"loc":"SAR","text":"On the eve of battle, I Adiutrix goes over to Aulus Vitellius."},{"t":22,"loc":"SAR","text":"Battle near Caralis: Aulus Vitellius wins against Marcus Salvius Otho."}],"rel":{"player|vindex":15,"macer|player":15,"galba|macer":-6,"macer|vindex":15,"F12|macer":-6,"F23|player":15,"F32|player":15,"F23|vitellius":15,"galba|vitellius":15,"F12|otho":-6,"vindex|vitellius":-3,"F32|F45":15,"F32|galba":-3,"F45|galba":-3,"F60|macer":-3,"player|vespasian":-15,"galba|vespasian":15,"otho|vespasian":15,"galba|otho":15,